From: CHEN Xuan <chenxuan@iscas.ac.cn>
Subject: [PATCH] comgr: use distribution LLVM and libc++ headers

Allow standalone builds to embed the installed libc++ headers rather than
requiring a complete LLVM source tree. This is a distribution path hook,
not an LLVM API or ABI compatibility workaround.

--- a/amd/comgr/cmake/LibcxxHeaders.cmake
+++ b/amd/comgr/cmake/LibcxxHeaders.cmake
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@

 # Find libc++ headers from the LLVM source tree
 set(LIBCXX_SEARCH_PATHS
+  "${COMGR_LIBCXX_INCLUDE_DIR}"
   "${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/libcxx/include"
   "${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/../libcxx/include"
   "${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/../../libcxx/include"  # amd/comgr -> libcxx
